            <ArticleTitle>Cancer pain guidelines: now that we have them, what do we do?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1229-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Addressing the what, who, when, where, and how of implementing the AHCPR guidelines is an attempt to simplify what may be an overwhelming process. Use the suggestions presented in Figure 1 to formulate an action plan, and remember to assign a time frame and individual accountability. The commitment to moving the guidelines from the bookshelf to the bedside begins now. Using a process such as this will assist efforts to improve care of patients in pain. It is our hope that a year from now the copy of the AHCPR cancer pain guidelines on your shelf will not be covered with dust but rather will be a well-worn text translated to practice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
